# Pairs with CausalOrder. Publishes the new floor paired with an offset read before the partition's last
# append, rather than atomically under the append gate, so the acked cursor can reach the offset while a
# write below the floor is still unacknowledged.
MODULE: CausalOrderFloorPublishedBeforeLastAppend
TARGET: CausalOrder
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the floor is published with an offset read before the last append, so S passes a write below the floor
PERTURBS: AdvanceFloor
BOUNDS: Parts = {1}

--- FIND
    /\ pub' = [pub EXCEPT ![p] = <<floor[p] + 1, Len(alog[p])>>]
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: the offset predates the last append.
    /\ pub' = [pub EXCEPT ![p] = <<floor[p] + 1, IF Len(alog[p]) > 0 THEN Len(alog[p]) - 1 ELSE 0>>]
--- END
